# Hand-maintained, macOS-only. This is the GLOBAL ignore file (git
# `core.excludesfile`): only put things here that no repo would ever want
# tracked, whatever the project. Anything project-specific belongs in that
# project's own .gitignore.
#
# Careful with bare extension globs: a rule like `*.d` also swallows
# directories such as `conf.d/`.

### macOS ###
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
Icon?

### Git ###
# Backups and conflict leftovers from merge tools
*.orig
*.BACKUP.*
*.BASE.*
*.LOCAL.*
*.REMOTE.*
*_BACKUP_*.txt
*_BASE_*.txt
*_LOCAL_*.txt
*_REMOTE_*.txt

### Editors ###
# Vim / Neovim
[._]*.s[a-v][a-z]
[._]*.sw[a-p]
!*.svg
Session.vim
Sessionx.vim
.netrwhist
[._]*.un~
tags

# Zed / VS Code — keep shared project config, drop the per-machine bits
.zed/*
!.zed/settings.json
!.zed/tasks.json
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.history/

### Environments & runtimes (see .config/mise/config.toml) ###
.direnv/
.env.local
.envrc.local

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Go
*.test
/vendor/

# Rust — `target/` only at the repo root; a nested `target/` may be real source
/target/

# C / C++ / CMake
*.o
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake-build-*/

### Claude Code ###
# Per-machine settings and scratch writes — never committed
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/.cc-writes/
**/AGENTS.local.md

### Serena ###
# Per-machine code-navigation index/config, set up by `clawd --onboard`
**/.serena/

### Graft ###
# Per-machine code-graph index, set up by `clawd --onboard` (see `graft init`)
**/graft/
